---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import FAQPageSchema from '../components/FAQPageSchema.astro';
import LocalBusinessSchema from '../components/LocalBusinessSchema.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';

const city = "Linden";
const latitude = 40.6209;
const longitude = -74.2373;

const faqs = [
  { q: "How far is AllStar from Linden?", a: "About 10 minutes up Route 1 and a few local roads. 1166 West Chestnut St, Union. Free parking on-site." },
  { q: "What programs are available?", a: "Adult BJJ, Muay Thai, and MMA (ages 16+). Kids Lions (7–13) and Cubs (4–6). Summer camp runs seasonally." },
  { q: "Do I need experience?", a: "No. Most students — adults and kids — start with none." },
  { q: "Can I watch a class before enrolling my child?", a: "Yes. Walk in any time. We don't hide what we do." },
  { q: "What's the free trial?", a: "Two weeks of unlimited classes. Adults can try any program. Kids can try their age group. No card required, no contract, no pressure." },
  { q: "How do I start?", a: "Fill out the form on this page or call (908) 341-1131. We'll text to confirm a class time." },
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Martial Arts in Linden, NJ — BJJ, Muay Thai & Kids Classes | AllStar"
  description="Martial arts classes for Linden, NJ families at AllStar Martial Arts in Union. BJJ, Muay Thai, MMA, and Kids programs. Renzo Gracie black belt. Free 2-week trial."
  ogImage="/images/adult-bjj-hero.jpg"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <LocalBusinessSchema city={city} latitude={latitude} longitude={longitude} />
    <FAQPageSchema faqs={faqs} />
  </Fragment>

  <PageHero
    eyebrow="10 minutes from Linden"
    headline="Martial Arts in Linden, NJ"
    sub="A straight 10-minute run up Route 1 into Union — BJJ, Muay Thai, MMA, and kids classes taught by a Renzo Gracie black belt. Free 2-week trial, no contract."
    bgImage="/images/adult-bjj-hero.jpg"
  />

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Drop onto Route 1 from downtown Linden and you're pulling into our lot in about ten minutes — no highway drama, just 1166 West Chestnut in Union with free parking out front. Linden training partners often carpool over with folks from neighboring <a href="/rahway/" class="text-brand-navy font-bold hover:text-brand-gold transition-colors">Rahway</a> and <a href="/roselle-park/" class="text-brand-navy font-bold hover:text-brand-gold transition-colors">Roselle Park →</a>, since the three towns blur together along the Route 1/9 corridor.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
        What keeps them making the drive is the coaching. Coach Jamal Patterson is a Renzo Gracie black belt, ADCC veteran, and former professional MMA fighter who competed in the IFL and Bellator, and that competition background changes how every technique gets broken down. Ask a Linden regular who's been here five or ten years — they'll tell you the difference shows up the second you step on the mat.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BJJ -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-brand-gray-light">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <div class="eyebrow">Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu</div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-black mb-5">BJJ Classes Near Linden, NJ</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu is our flagship. Adults 16 and up, beginners welcome — most people who walk through the door from Linden have never rolled a day in their life, and that's exactly who the beginner curriculum is built for.
      </p>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Yes, other schools around Linden teach BJJ, and a few even share our Renzo Gracie lineage. The separator is the person running the room. Jamal's résumé — ADCC, IFL, Bellator, UWC champion — isn't a poster on the wall; it's baked into how he teaches every grip, sweep, and submission. New to it entirely? Our <a href="/adult-bjj/" class="text-brand-navy font-bold hover:text-brand-gold transition-colors">adult BJJ program →</a> is the front door.
      </p>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
        Evening classes run at 6, 7, and 8 PM most weekdays — scheduled around the NJ Transit commute and adults getting home late off the North Jersey Coast Line. Two weeks free. No contract.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Kids -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <div class="eyebrow">Kids Martial Arts</div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-black mb-5">Kids Martial Arts Near Linden, NJ</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5">
        <div class="bg-brand-gray-light p-6 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-brand-gold">
          <h3 class="text-xl text-brand-black mb-2">Cubs — Ages 4–6</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-gray text-sm leading-relaxed">Preschool-age energy with martial arts structure. Focus on coordination, listening, and confidence. Short activities, high engagement, constant positive reinforcement.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-brand-gray-light p-6 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-brand-navy">
          <h3 class="text-xl text-brand-black mb-2">Lions — Ages 7–13</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-gray text-sm leading-relaxed">Real Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu technique. Takedowns, escapes, positions. These kids are not doing karate katas — they're learning a system that works. Parents consistently report that the confidence carries into school.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mt-5">
        For a lot of Linden families, the draw is bully prevention that actually holds up. When a kid from Linden High or one of the local elementary schools knows they can handle themselves, the whole dynamic with a bully shifts — usually without a single punch being thrown.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Muay Thai + MMA -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-brand-navy text-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-4xl">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow text-brand-gold">Muay Thai</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">Muay Thai Near Linden, NJ</h2>
          <p class="text-white/90 leading-relaxed">
            This is the one nobody else in the area runs. Across the Linden, Union, and Rahway stretch, no other gym pairs authentic Muay Thai instruction with BJJ under one roof. Real pad work, real technique, real conditioning — and beginners are genuinely welcome, not thrown to the wolves.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow text-brand-gold">MMA</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">MMA Classes Near Linden, NJ</h2>
          <p class="text-white/90 leading-relaxed">
            Our MMA program welds BJJ, Muay Thai, and wrestling into one complete game. It's coached by Jamal Patterson — a pro fighter who has cornered UFC athletes from their amateur debut all the way to the big show. Adults 16 and up.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Landmarks -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <div class="eyebrow">If you know Linden</div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-brand-black mb-5">You Know These Spots — We're 10 Minutes Away</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {["Downtown Linden", "Linden Public Library", "Route 1 North", "Tremley Point Road", "Linden High School", "Warinanco Park", "NJ Transit bus hub", "Linden Train Station area"].map((l) => (
          <span class="bg-brand-gray-light text-brand-gray px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm">📍 {l}</span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQ items={faqs} />

  <CTA
    headline="Two Weeks Free — Linden Families Welcome"
    sub="Show up. Bring water. We'll handle the rest. No commitment, no pressure."
  />
</PageLayout>
